# codebase-consistency-hooks
#
# After editing any source file, run the pattern consistency check and
# address any findings before considering the task complete.
#
# COMMAND
#   python3 scripts/check_pattern_consistency.py --format text
#
# EXIT CODES
#   0  Clean — no divergence from existing conventions. Proceed.
#   1  Findings — output explains which file, what the dominant convention
#      is, and which existing files to follow. Fix the flagged file to match,
#      then re-run to confirm clean before finishing.
#   2  Internal error in the checker itself — safe to ignore and proceed.
#
# STRUCTURED OUTPUT (useful when planning fixes across multiple files)
#   python3 scripts/check_pattern_consistency.py --format json
#
# LLM-ENRICHED OUTPUT (requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in environment)
#   The checker calls the API automatically when the key is present.
#   No extra flags needed.
#
# CHECKS PERFORMED
#   error_handling_style     — reraise vs swallow vs log_and_continue
#   logging_call             — logger vs logging vs print vs console.*
#   naming_convention        — snake_case vs camelCase vs PascalCase
#   docstring_coverage       — documented vs undocumented (.py only)
#   import_organization      — grouped (isort) vs flat
#   type_annotation_coverage — typed vs untyped (.py / .ts / .tsx)
#   return_consistency       — explicit_return vs implicit_return
#
# TUNING (optional — place consistency.json at repo root)
#   {
#     "majority_threshold": 0.6,
#     "checks": { "docstring_coverage": false }
#   }
